            <ArticleTitle>[Study on metabolites from a sponge-derived fungus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3374-3378</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.19540/j.cnki.cjcmm.2017.0131</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have carried out the investigation on a sponge-derived fungus,which was identified as Emericella variecolor from the south sea of China. Two new chemical constituents,(+)-2-acetyl-dihydroterrein (1) and (+)-3-acetyl-dihydroterrein (2),with four known compounds,anditomin (3),andilesin A (4),andilesin C (5) and andilesin B (6),were isolated from this fungus by column chromatography over silica gel, Sephadex LH-20, and ODS. The structures of 1 and 2 were elucidated by spectroscopic methods including NMR,HR-ESI-MS,and CD.</AbstractText>
